// Canonical owner-controlled syntax registry (I7).
// The reference comparison is temporary and is not a generator dependency.
//
// This file holds the marker syntax only. Marker names are not syntax: each
// marker is a struct of Compiler/Prelude/Markers.jet (MARKER_SOURCE), the one
// marker registry, and no list here copies them.

/// The sole prefix for applying a typed rule. A rule may target a
/// declaration, expression, or brace scope when that rule declares the target
/// legal. Supersedes the former marker-plane reservation: `x.reflect()` reads
/// compiler facts (`T.reflect().layout`, `build.target.os`), prefix `@` marks only a
/// live link, and infix `@` remains the package-source reference.
///
/// `#` has two other jobs, told apart by parser position only (no lookahead
/// heuristics): inside a bracketed type, `[T#N]`, it is the fixed-size-list
/// separator (S76 `TYPE_FIXED_SIZE_SEP`); after a package name it is the
/// version-pin separator (`pkg#1.2.0`, same constant). Keeps all three jobs on
/// one token.
RULE_PREFIX: "#"

/// Writes one of a declaration's markers as a line inside its body:
/// `#X: value`, alone on its line, directly in the body of a struct, enum,
/// trait, impl, module or function. `#X: true` applies `#X` with no
/// arguments, `#X: false` is `#!X`, `#X: v` passes one simple argument
/// (a name path, string or number) and `#X: (args)` passes any other list.
/// The line is the same marker as `#X(args)` above the declaration; one
/// declaration writes its whole set in one place.
MARKER_INBODY_SEPARATOR: ":"
